		"readme" : "Every editor ID in customkeywords is registered when you click 'Load Keywords from File' on the Armor MCM page. Load REPLACES the registered set (confirmation first): keywords not in this file are dropped. Registering or removing keywords in the MCM never changes this file - click 'Save Keywords to File' to write your registered set to the TOP of customkeywords (existing entries stay in place). copyuprespectlimit holds the rest of the Advanced Nudity Detection set - move IDs into customkeywords to enable them. IMPORTANT: key names in this file must stay lowercase (PapyrusUtil looks keys up lowercased; a key like 'CustomKeywords' is silently ignored) - the editor ID values keep their case. Long IDs work here (no SkyUI 30-char cap). Registered keywords are managed per armor through the Add/Remove keyword menus on the Armor page; the pick-lists scroll, so there is no hard display cap. Still keep the set lean: every registered keyword makes those lists longer and adds work to the keyword restore that runs on every game load. The shipped default is 22 female-oriented keywords (graded exposure, pasties, skimpy garments + the Modesty set) - male variants live below, copy them up for male characters."
